<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 29,683,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 29,683,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, meal exports in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 11/20/96    11/13/96	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 29,683,000  30,145,000    28,177,000</p>
<p> Capacity-X	34,948,000  34,476,000    33,569,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,140,728  34,668,921	     N/A</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 133,818     132,305	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   11/20/96    11/13/96     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,289,000   5,321,000     5,073,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    5,025,000   4,838,000     4,598,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  4,837,000   5,143,000     4,894,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,178,000   3,209,000     2,782,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,017,000   4,185,000     3,750,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,346,000   5,224,000     5,207,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,991,000   2,226,000     1,873,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	29,683,000  30,145,000    28,177,000</p>
